From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Liana <liana@lianas.org>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 10:36:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] systemd: open host root O_PATH in chaseat()

Since 874971b1c0 ("chase: wire up XAT_FDROOT", v260), chaseat() anchors
host-root resolution with open("/", O_DIRECTORY|O_RDONLY). Every later
use of that fd is openat(O_PATH) or statx(AT_EMPTY_PATH), so read access
on / is never needed, but Landlock (LANDLOCK_ACCESS_FS_READ_DIR) and
AppArmor deny it. sd-device then fails "Failed to get target of
/sys/class/hidraw/...", libudev enumerates nothing, and Firefox WebAuthn
cannot see FIDO keys inside a landlocked house.

Open / with O_PATH, matching v259 and main (79862d33a0, v261).

Link: https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/41630
Link: https://github.com/systemd/systemd/pull/42012
---
 src/basic/chase.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/basic/chase.c b/src/basic/chase.c
index 82946ea..ee60e37 100644
--- a/src/basic/chase.c
+++ b/src/basic/chase.c
@@ -278,7 +278,7 @@ int chaseat(int dir_fd, const char *path, ChaseFlags flags, char **ret_path, int
                         goto success;
                 }
 
-                _dir_fd = open("/", O_DIRECTORY|O_RDONLY|O_CLOEXEC);
+                _dir_fd = open("/", O_DIRECTORY|O_PATH|O_CLOEXEC);
                 if (_dir_fd < 0)
                         return -errno;
 
-- 
